        "criticism": "Critics of judicial activism argue that it undermines the democratic process by allowing unelected judges to make decisions that should be left to the legislative branch. They believe that the judiciary's role should be limited to interpreting laws as they are written, without injecting personal or political biases into their decisions."
      },
      "constitution_interpretation": {
        "living_document": "Some view the Constitution as a living document that should be interpreted in light of contemporary values and circumstances, supporting the idea that the Supreme Court can and should adapt the law to meet the evolving needs of society.",
